<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 19 September, from 634 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/634">634 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,392 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Rashidun Arabs under Khalid ibn al-Walid take Damascus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege begun on 21 August, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> fell to the forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalid-ibn-al-walid">Khalid ibn al-Walid</a>. It was the first major city of the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> to fall in the Muslim conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalid-ibn-al-walid">Khalid ibn al-Walid</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1356">1356 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">670 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Black Prince captures King John II at Poitiers</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-black-prince">Edward the Black Prince</a>'s outnumbered army defeated the French at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> II. His huge ransom and the chaos that followed brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> to the brink of collapse.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1410">1410 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">616 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Polish-Lithuanian siege of Marienburg ends in failure</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After two months, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Władysław II Jagiełło</a> and Grand Duke Vytautas lifted their siege of Marienburg (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malbork">Malbork</a>), capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Knights</a>, meant to complete the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> after their victory at Grunwald. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-von-plauen">Heinrich von Plauen</a> led the defence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-of-the-kingdom-of-poland">Crown of the Kingdom of Poland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1622">1622 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">404 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Heidelberg Castle surrenders to Tilly's Imperial-Spanish army</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg-castle">Heidelberg Castle</a> surrendered to the Imperial-Spanish army of the Count of Tilly and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-fernandez-de-cordoba">Gonzalo Fernández de Córdoba</a>, three days after the city, capital of the Palatinate, was stormed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-tserclaes-count-of-tilly">Johann Tserclaes, Count of Tilly</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palatinate-region">Palatinate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jamestown.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1676">1676 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">350 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nathaniel Bacon's rebels burn Jamestown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rebels led by Nathaniel Bacon burned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>'s capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a>, in a revolt against Governor Berkeley. Their alliance of poor whites, servants and enslaved Africans alarmed the colony's elite.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1796">1796 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">230 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington's Farewell Address is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Washington announced he would not seek a third term in an address printed in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a> newspaper. He warned against party faction and permanent foreign alliances.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1881">1881 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">145 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President James Garfield dies 79 days after being shot</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Garfield died of infection and complications from the wound inflicted by Charles Guiteau. His doctors' unsterile probing of the wound almost certainly contributed to his death.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hikers find Ötzi the Iceman in the Alps</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two German hikers found a body in the ice on the Austrian-Italian border. Ötzi proved to be a man who died some 5,300 years ago, killed by an arrow, with his clothes and tools preserved.</p></div></li></ol>
